**The truth about the RA Bachelors Program**

(Via propeller post: https://propeller.fullsail.com:443/index.cfm?fa=discussion.showPosts&t=31837&f=219) I was very excited to learn that soon there might be an option to enroll in a Bachelors Degree Program for Recording Arts. Soon, the main Full Sail website boasted the new degree as well as a list of classes offered in the program. Advanced Recording, Advanced Post, Mic Theory, Game Audio; the list of new classes was impressive and I was looking forward to enrolling in the new program. The Truth: To the RA students currently in the Associates program who would like to enter the bachelor's 'completer's course,' here are the actual classes we would be taking: Month 1: Vocal Production & Physics Month 2: Interactive Audio & English Month 3: Advanced Interactive Audio & Professional Writing Month 4: Music Production and Arr. & Statistics and Analysis Month 5: Digital Mastering The Cost: $22,285

